  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="14">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VIAtr">VI Atr</ref> 14</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="14">[Not in D]</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="14" corresp="#wit-k">⁊ sy ælc cyricgrið binnan wagum ⁊ cyninges handgrið efen unwemme.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And sy ælc cyricgrið binnan wagum and cyninges handgrið efenunwemme.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-k">And every right of sanctuary within the walls of a church, and the protection granted by the king in person shall remain equally inviolate.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-k">And all sanctuary within church walls and the sanctuary received from the hand of a Christian king are to remain equally inviolable.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Und jeder Kirchenfriede innerhalb der Mauern und des Königs Handfriede bestehe gleich unverletzlich.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And let every church's protection within its walls and the king's personally given protection be equally inviolable.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="250">[?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">Vgl. [?]</note>
        <note type="comparisonIncomplete">Some of Liebermann’s notes here are cut off in the gutter of the scan used, and are still to be completed.</note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#liebermann"><ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_1-1">VIII Atr 1.1</ref>; <ref target="clause:VIIIAtr_3">VIII Atr 3</ref>; <ref target="clause:ICn_2-2">I Cn 2.2</ref></note>
        <note type="editorial">14 is missing from the Latin paraphrase and the source, so perhaps interpolated by K (Liebermann).</note>
      </div>
    </body>
